      "id": "wsd9j8o",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. Meaning and Importance of DPSP"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Directive Principles of State Policy (DPSP) are contained in Part IV of the Indian Constitution.",
        "DPSPs are broadly classified into Socialist, Gandhian, and Liberal–Intellectual principles.",
        "Unlike Fundamental Rights, Directive Principles are non-justiciable in nature.",
        "DPSPs aim to establish social and economic democracy in the country."
      ],
      "id": "9a4o3ee"
    },
